<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caeco</span></b> , āvi, ātum, 1,
			v. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				make blind</i>, <i>to blind.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sol caecat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 325</span></i>
			 (300); <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. Nat. S. Fel.
				20, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">20, 292</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unde caecatus est (Appius Claudius),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
						Vict. Vir. Ill. 34, 3</span></i>
			.—Hence, in gardening: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculum,</span>”
				<i>to destroy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 9, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 24, 16</span></i>;
			cf. caecus, I. C., and oculus.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui largitione caecarunt mentes imperitorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 66, 139</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut (animi acies) ne caecetur erroribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 5, 13, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecati libidinibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 30, 72</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cupiditate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Dom. 23, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecata mens subito terrore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 6, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectora... serie caecata laborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 2, 7, 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecabitur spes vindemiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 6, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">timidos artus,</span>”
				<i>to make senseless</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. Cul. 198</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to make dark</i>,
				<i>to obscure</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecantur silvae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Avien. Per. 504</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of 
			 discourse: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">celeritate caecata oratio,</span>”
				<i>rendered obscure</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 76, 264</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
